{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_34","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"rg -n 'probe|port 9|8788|default-src|javascript.*error' docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r76.stream -o --replace '\"'$0'\"' | head -10; cat /private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/../tasks/by2or0blt.output; ls -la /Users/lchingen/.claude/projects/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109.jsonl; ls -t /private/tmp | head -60\"","aggregated_output":"12:default-src\n12:javascript:` | shown as text, never a link |\\n    78\\t| Text holding `</script>`, `<img onerror=…>`, `&` or U+2028 | the embed escapes it, the page shows it as text, and the JSON parses back identical |\\n    79\\t| The page is opened from disk, a static host or any path | it reads only its embedded data; nothing else exists to read |\\n    80\\t| The browser blocks inline script | nothing renders. The page shows a `<noscript>` line saying it needs script. It holds no forecast to leak |\\n    81\\t| A page edited after the build (a fetch added, a field added) | `check_package` refuses: the bytes differ from `render_page(data)` |\\n    82\\t| The template changes in a later version | old packages fail `check_package` under the new code by design; a new template is a new format version |\\n    83\\t| A dark scheme and a phone width | the style handles both; checked in the browser check |\\n    84\\t\\n    85\\t## 3. Value × reader\\n    86\\t\\n    87\\t- Every value the page shows comes from the embedded data; the page reads no other value.\\n    88\\t- The page's readers are a person's browser and the browser check.\\n    89\\t- The data's readers are unchanged from slice 1: `check_package`, `check_origins`, the tests. The page adds one reader of the data,\\n    90\\t  the page script, and no new writer.\\n    91\\t\\n    92\\t## 4. New path × old checks\\n    93\\t\\n    94\\t| Slice-1 check | Slice 2 |\\n    95\\t|---|---|\\n    96\\t| Closed set of the data, origin check, staged check before the no-replace publication, the no-replace report | unchanged |\\n    97\\t| The manifest's closed set | gains `page_sha256`; `format` becomes `hivemind-release/2` |\\n    98\\t| Exactly the package files, each read once, no links, no pipes | the same rule over three files |\\n    99\\t| The literal-values rule of verification (council 75d) | applied to the page checks as well |\\n   100\\t\\n   101\\t## 5. Tests (`tests/test_release.py`) and mutants\\n   102\\t\\n   103\\t1. **Determinism.** `render_page` of the fixture data twice gives the same bytes. The page holds the data bytes, escaped as specified.\\n   104\\t2. **Escaping.** A fixture quote holding `</script><img src=x onerror=alert(1)>` and a U+2028:\\n   105\\t   - the page has no second `<script>` start in the data block;\\n   106\\t   - parsing the embedded JSON back gives the data unchanged.\\n   107\\t3. **No network code.** The template's script contains none of the listed APIs. Its CSP is exactly the policy above, with the hashes\\n   108\\t   of its own script and style.\\n   109\\t4. **The package check:**\\n   110\\t   - a page changed by one byte, with the manifest hash refreshed, is refused with its exact reason;\\n   111\\t   - a page with `fetch(\\\"http://127.0.0.1:8788/library\\\")` added, its CSP hash and manifest hash both updated, is refused, because it\\n   112\\t     is not `render_page(data)`;\\n   113\\t   - a missing page and a fourth file are each refused.\\n   114\\t5. **Literal identifiers:** `hivemind-release/2` and `release-allow-list/1`.\\n   115\\t\\n   116\\t**Mutants:**\\n   117\\t- `render_page` not escaping `<`;\\n   118\\t- the script using `innerHTML` for the quote;\\n   119\\t- a source link without the http(s) test;\\n   120\\t- `check_package` not comparing the page with `render_page`;\\n   121\\t- the CSP hash computed over a different script.\\n   122\\t\\n   123\\t## 6. The $0 screen check (`release_screen.mjs`, run once)\\n   124\\t\\n   125\\t- **Setup.** Headless Chrome from `/Applications/Google Chrome.app`, driven through its DevTools protocol with Node's built-in\\n   126\\t  WebSocket, on a fresh profile in the scratchpad. Each page is opened from `file://`.\\n   127\\t- **Packages:** `old-1` at its default day, and the two dated leak packages (`old-3` at 2026-08-25, `old-1` at 2026-08-28), built by\\n   128\\t  the slice-1 command under format 2.\\n   129\\t\\n   130\\t**Recorded for each page:**\\n   131\\t- the page's own network requests (`Network.requestWillBeSent` for the page target). Only the document itself may appear;\\n   132\\t- console error\n12:8788\n13:probe\n16:probe\n16:8788\n16:probe\n16:probe\n16:probe\n16:8788\n1 failed, 428 passed in 66.87s (0:01:06)\nrelease check: every acceptance item and budget met; diagnostic hits to read by hand: {'old-1': 1378, 'old-2': 771, 'old-3': 1613, 'served': 1794}\n\n[exited with code 0]\n-rw-------@ 1 lchingen  staff  346682967 Nov 23 12:11 /Users/lchingen/.claude/projects/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109.jsonl\nls: codex-daemon-501: Operation not permitted\npytest-of-lchingen\nzeb_def_ipc_58871\nzeb_def_ipc_35502\nzeb_def_ipc_1885\nzeb_def_ipc_811\ntmpcsm5bv8a\ntmpphi3wbu7\ntmploz66ox1\ntmpo9mqccxc\ntmpdyen0sqp\ntmpq9jeeo30\ntmpuh4n86oq\ntmprhldl35x\ntmpnfww_heq\ntmphw59_ryt\ntmpz4z8_c7s\ntmpc0vtx26y\ntmpvfzrkyz1\ntmp0z78zee5\ntmpf649zt7v\ntmpg3bhkgck\ntmpc2bc6_3c\ntmp9e9irjke\ntmpl_kyj23t\ntmpg853tko0\ntmpx1mlegzi\ntmpli0sbazq\ntmpka2wyykk\ntmpp3pr7sn9\ntmphcv3vf77\ntmpevnsgrai\ntmpobyj044l\ntmpy92kt8ms\ntmpoo1urhj6\ntmpdp58i1fm\ntmpi8v5lv0p\ntmp5wsuabyj\ntmpt7c5cf55\ntmpc2b36qq6\ntmpozr56roq\ntmp2x6ydkzn\ntmpct_0vjv6\ntmpq2wb1b_7\ntmpeocbbhmr\ntmpbhl97a_r\ntmpociu0wud\ntmpwblqbcls\ntmp4jt6npy9\ntmpo8n3zlm4\ntmp47wwe__2\ntmpjwsvc3ag\ntmpk1syqf7v\ntmpfvfp4hni\ntmppuih6cii\ntmpblamf375\ntmp5g85tlzh\ntmpcwcx8on8\ntmp7xr4_cpa\ntmpd8j3eijk\ntmpd5v