CSP hash over another script: 2 failing: test_27_the_template_has_no_network_code_drawn_text_or_clipping, test_29_the_page_template_is_the_one_the_screen_run_certified\n37 of 38 mutants caught\n120140 429 passed in 67.36s (0:01:07)\nrelease check: every acceptance item and budget met; diagnostic hits to read by hand: {'old-1': 1378, 'old-2': 771, 'old-3': 1613, 'served': 1794}\ncontrol: PASS 40 passed in 2.84s\nMISSED  canonical-day check removed: 0 failing: \n37 of 38 mutants caught 429 passed in 67.36s (0:01:07)\nrelease check: every acceptance item and budget met; diagnostic hits to read by hand: {'old-1': 1378, 'old-2': 771, 'old-3': 1613, 'served': 1794}\ncontrol: PASS 40 passed in 2.84s\nMISSED  canonical-day check removed: 0 failing: \n37 of 38 mutants caught\n     1\t**Ready to build.** Revision 7 closes both 76g findings in the design. Browser acceptance remains ahead.\n     2\t\n     3\t1. **Contrast lookup — closed.** The check starts at the element holding the text and walks upward only if its background is transparent. The decisive test requires “Forecast unavailable” to fail when its dark text sits on its own dark background inside a light card. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:237](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:237) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:274](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:274)\n     4\t2. **Whole-page template pin — closed.** The renderer inserts escaped data into the complete template’s single placeholder. After browser certification, the test records the SHA-256 of that template with the placeholder intact. Changing only the fallback sentence therefore fails the test. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:8](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:8) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:176](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:176)\n     5\t\n     6\t**Optional.** Further tests for hypothetical CSS changes remain optional because those edits already change the complete template’s hash. [codex-r76g.md:7](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r76g.md:7)     1\t**Not ready to build as written.** Revision 6 closes the clipping finding. Two gaps remain in what the design can certify before shipping. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:224](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:224) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:227](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:227) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:167](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:167)\n     2\t\n     3\t1. **Clipping is closed. Contrast is still open.** The browser check walks the quote’s ancestors, so a one-line wrapper with `contain: paint` fails even when Morningstar’s quote wraps normally inside it. The contrast check starts its background lookup one element too high. If “Forecast unavailable” has dark text on its **own** dark background inside a light card, line 228 compares the dark text with the light card. That can pass while the reader sees a blank marker. Start the lookup at the element holding the text. The decisive test is that same marker on a contrasting parent. This matters on the first certification, before any hashes are pinned. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:224](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:224) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:228](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:228) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:261](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:261)\n     4\t\n     5\t2. **The pin leaves the surrounding HTML uncovered.** For an unchanged, certified template and accepted package data, I found no separate forecast leak or outgoing request path. The data is escaped, source addresses are plain text, and the package checker compares the page byte for byte. But that comparison uses the *current* `render_page`, and the two test hashes cover only the style and script. Changing the static fallback sentence, for example, changes what a reader sees when JavaScript is blocked. Both hashes stay identical, and a newly built package still equals the current renderer. Pin the complete template with its data placeholder intact. A change to the fallback alone should then fail the pin. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:72](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:72) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:79](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:79) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:90](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:90) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:101](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:101) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:167](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:167)\n     6\t\n     7\t**Convergence.** These two corrections cover the page first certified and the page later shipped. Further checks for hypothetical CSS changes that would already fail the complete-template pin are optional. This was a read-only design review. The browser acceptance run is still ahead. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:3) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:186](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:186)total 63816\ndrwxr-xr-x@   9 lchingen  wheel       288 Nov 23 11:52 draft\ndrwxr-xr-x@   5 lchingen  wheel       160 Nov 23 11:41 cdp\ndrwx------@ 343 lchingen  wheel     10976 Nov 23 11:41 .\ndrwxr-xr-x@   5 lchingen  wheel       160 Nov 23 11:39 headless\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  wheel       511 Nov 23 10:38 full-suite.log\ndrwxr-xr-x@   4 lchingen  wheel       128 Nov 23 10:36 canonical-day\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  wheel      7195 Nov 23 10:34 release_mutants.py\ndrwxr-xr-x@   5 lchingen  wheel       160 Nov 23 10:24 link-test\ndrwxr-xr-x@   7 lchingen  wheel       224 Nov 23 10:17 renamex-test\ndrwxr-xr-x@   5 lchingen  wheel       160 Nov 23 10:13 rename-test\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  wheel      1685 Nov 23 10:05 oneline_census.py\n-rw-r--r--@   1 lchingen  wheel      2544 Nov 23 09:58 release_census.py\ndrwxr-xr-x@  14 lchingen  wheel       448 Nov 23 08:00 second-week\ndrwxr-xr-x@   3 lchingen  wheel        96 Nov 23 08:00 mutants-retry\ndrwxr-xr-x@   6 lchingen  wheel       192 Nov 23 08:00 chain-dry-6\ndrwxr-xr-x@   6 lchingen  wheel       192 Nov 23 08:00 chain-dry-8\ndrwxr-xr-x@   6 lchingen  wheel       192 Nov 23 08:00 chain-dry-9\ndrwxr-xr-x@   6 lchingen  wheel       192 Nov 23 08:00 chain-dry-7\ndrwxr-xr-x@   6 lchingen  wheel       192 Nov 23 08:00 chain-dry\ndrwxr-xr-x@  10 lchingen  wheel       320 Nov 23 08:00 step2-lines\ndrwxr-xr-x@   6 lchingen  wheel       192 Nov 23 08:00 chain-dry-10\ndrwxr-xr-x@   6 lchingen  wheel       192 Nov 23 08:00 chain-dry-17\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
