{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_39","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba tests/test_release.py | sed -n '388,430p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r76b.md | head -18; nl -ba poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-expected.json | head -48; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/round77-brief.md | head -60; ls -lat poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/.chrome-orQCzT | head -5\"","aggregated_output":"   388\t    \"\"\"§6 test 13: the items copy lacks item-3; the package copy drops every item-3 source, keeping e2 with none, its hash refreshed.\n   389\t    A checker that silently skips a missing item accepts this pair; the release refuses it, naming the item.\"\"\"\n   390\t    out = tmp_path / 'release'\n   391\t    data = build_package(stores, out)\n   392\t    short = make_items(tmp_path / 'short.sqlite', ids=('item-1', 'item-2'))\n   393\t    copy = tmp_path / 'copy'\n   394\t    shutil.copytree(out, copy)\n   395\t    for piece in by_id(data)['v1']['evidence']:      # e1 loses its item-3 source, e2 keeps its record with no source: what a checker\n   396\t        piece['sources'] = [s for s in piece['sources'] if s['uri'] != 'https://example.com/article-3']   # that drops missing items expects\n   397\t    rewrite_data(copy, data)\n   398\t    refused_with(lambda: check((stores[0], short), copy), 'evidence e1: source item item-3 is not in the items database')\n   399\t\n   400\t\n   401\tdef test_15_symbolic_links_and_repeated_member_names_are_refused(stores, tmp_path):\n   402\t    \"\"\"§6 test 15: a symbolic link, a repeated member name and a named pipe are refused (the pipe without waiting).\"\"\"\n   403\t    out = tmp_path / 'release'\n   404\t    build_package(stores, out)\n   405\t    linked = tmp_path / 'linked'\n   406\t    shutil.copytree(out, linked)\n   407\t    (tmp_path / 'outside.json').write_bytes((linked / release.DATA_FILE).read_bytes())\n   408\t    (linked / release.DATA_FILE).unlink()\n   409\t    (linked / release.DATA_FILE).symlink_to(tmp_path / 'outside.json')\n   410\t    refused_with(lambda: check(stores, linked), f'{linked}/release-data.json: not a regular file')\n   411\t    repeated = tmp_path / 'repeated'\n   412\t    shutil.copytree(out, repeated)\n   413\t    raw = (repeated / release.DATA_FILE).read_bytes()\n   414\t    genuine = b'\"one_line\":\"Morningstar estimates $361 billion of revenue for the year.\"'\n   415\t    assert raw.count(genuine) == 1\n   416\t    payload = raw.replace(genuine, b'\"one_line\":\"About $390 billion\",' + genuine)\n   417\t    (repeated / release.DATA_FILE).write_bytes(payload)\n   418\t    manifest = json.loads((repeated / release.MANIFEST_FILE).read_text())\n   419\t    manifest['data_sha256'] = hashlib.sha256(payload).hexdigest()\n   420\t    (repeated / release.MANIFEST_FILE).write_text(json.dumps(manifest))\n   421\t    refused_with(lambda: check(stores, repeated), \"a JSON member name repeats: ['one_line']\")\n   422\t    piped = tmp_path / 'piped'\n   423\t    shutil.copytree(out, piped)\n   424\t    (piped / release.DATA_FILE).unlink()\n   425\t    os.mkfifo(piped / release.DATA_FILE)\n   426\t    result = run('check', piped, '--ledger', stores[0], '--items', stores[1], timeout=30)      # a blocking open would hang here\n   427\t    assert result.returncode == 1\n   428\t    stderr_line(result, f'refused: ReleaseRefused: {piped}/release-data.json: not a regular file')\n   429\t\n   430\t\n     1\t**Not ready to build.** A `v8` card could show both “Forecast unavailable” and “Forecast: $361 billion” and pass the proposed screen check. The $361 billion is a genuine Morningstar estimate. Showing it separately as Hivemind’s forecast would change what the reader sees while leaving every checked field correct. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:174](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:174) · [RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:124](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-CHECK-RESULT.md:124)\n     2\t\n     3\t| Round-76 finding | Revision-2 assessment |\n     4\t|---|---|\n     5\t| 1. Source links | **Closed.** Addresses render as plain text. The expanded-page check requires zero links, `href` attributes, or `src` attributes. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:82](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:82) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:179](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:179) |\n     6\t| 2. Embedded JSON | **Closed.** The literal escapes and header order are explicit. The browser must show the fixture’s exact quote after expansion and find zero image elements. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:48](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:48) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:189](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:189) |\n     7\t| 3. Format 2 and package checks | **Closed in design.** The checker hashes and compares the same page bytes, and a wrong page hash alone must fail. The instruction to regenerate the page for altered test data applies to both existing helpers, including the one in the test suite. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:114](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:114) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:130](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:130) · [test_release.py:180](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:180) |\n     8\t| 4. What the cards actually show | **Still open.** Revision 2 pins all 1,284 `v8` entries, preserves genuine uses of “Bullish,” and checks reopening. Two gaps remain below. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:165](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:165) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:173](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:173) |\n     9\t| 5. Blocked fetch | **Closed.** Observation starts before navigation. The altered script must render the normal list, and Chrome must name both the intended address and `connect-src` in its security error. I found no further request path in the specified page. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:158](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:158) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:192](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:192) |\n    10\t| 6. Browser acceptance conditions | **Partly closed.** The fallback, navigation start time, and 390-pixel width check are concrete. The timer still stops when the list exists in the DOM, which can precede visibility. The dark-background check also lacks a fixed expected colour. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:40](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:40) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:205](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:205) · [tokens.css:3](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/web/design-system/tokens.css:3) |\n    11\t\n    12\t**Two corrections are needed before build.**\n    13\t\n    14\t1. **Check the whole visible card.** Reading named elements and searching the remaining text for five labels, five conditions, and one forecast prefix lets the extra “Forecast: $361 billion” line pass. Compare the complete visible `v8` card with its expected contents, collapsed and expanded, preserving the grouping of each quote with its sources. A decisive test is to add that one visible line while leaving every named element intact. Use the same visibility requirement for the timer’s end point so a hidden list cannot meet the three-second budget. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:176](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:176) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:180](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:180) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:210](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:210)\n    15\t2. **Take each dated card’s expected contents from its own accepted package.** Line 166 names only the default September 20 `old-1` package. I checked the stored files. Its `v36` asks about MediaTek financing. The August 25 `old-3/v36` asks whether NVIDIA will begin shipping Rubin Ultra. Each dated card has exactly one evidence entry, yet both proposed checks could pass with an empty expanded panel because they ask only whether forbidden phrases are absent. Freeze each day, question, answer, and single evidence entry from its dated package, then require that entry and its source to be visible. The existing acceptance script identifies both package paths. [RELEASE-PAGE.md:165](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:165) · [RELEASE-PAGE.md:184](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:184) · [release_check.py:208](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_check.py:208)\n    16\t\n    17\t**Optional.** Choose the literal dark background before the first run. The referenced stylesheet defines `--ink` as `#0f140d` and declares a light colour scheme. If `--ink` is the intended dark background, the browser check can expect `rgb(15, 20, 13)` directly. [tokens.css:8](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/web/design-system/tokens.css:8) · [tokens.css:21](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/web/design-system/tokens.css:21)\n    18\t\n     1\t{\n     2\t \"accepted\": \"/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23g\",\n     3\t \"pages\": {\n     4\t  \"old-1/v8\": {\n     5\t   \"count\": 47,\n     6\t   \"collapsed\": {\n     7\t    \"header\": [\n     8\t     \"Hivemind release\",\n     9\t     \"As of 2026-09-20\",\n    10\t     \"19 number questions · 28 event questions · 0 Yes/No questions\"\n    11\t    ],\n    12\t    \"cards\": [\n    13\t     {\n    14\t      \"id\": \"v1\",\n    15\t      \"top\": [\n    16\t       \"How much credit support for AI clouds will NVIDIA have committed at the end of FY2027?\",\n    17\t       \"Open\",\n    18\t       \"Forecast unavailable\",\n    19\t       \"630 pieces of evidence\"\n    20\t      ],\n    21\t      \"groups\": []\n    22\t     },\n    23\t     {\n    24\t      \"id\": \"v2\",\n    25\t      \"top\": [\n    26\t       \"What total amount of NVIDIA’s credit-support and capacity-purchase obligations will be outstanding at the FY2027 annual report?\",\n    27\t       \"Open\",\n    28\t       \"Forecast unavailable\",\n    29\t       \"647 pieces of evidence\"\n    30\t      ],\n    31\t      \"groups\": []\n    32\t     },\n    33\t     {\n    34\t      \"id\": \"v3\",\n    35\t      \"top\": [\n    36\t       \"Will NVIDIA begin shipping its Rubin platform by December 31, 2026?\",\n    37\t       \"Open\",\n    38\t       \"Answer: Yes\",\n    39\t       \"394 pieces of evidence\"\n    40\t      ],\n    41\t      \"groups\": []\n    42\t     },\n    43\t     {\n    44\t      \"id\": \"v4\",\n    45\t      \"top\": [\n    46\t       \"What will NVIDIA's total revenue be in FY2027?\",\n    47\t       \"Open\",\n    48\t       \"Forecast unavailable\",\n     1\t# Council round 77: review the built slice 2 (the reader's page) against its design, and its $0 result (read-only)\n     2\t\n     3\tYou are an independent reviewer. Do not edit any file. The repository is /Users/lchingen/hivemind. Cite file:line.\n     4\t\n     5\tSlice 2 was built to `docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md` revision 7, which council 76h found ready. The pieces:\n     6\t- `src/hivemind/release.py`: `page_template`, `render_page`, `embed`, the format-2 `write_package` and `check_package`;\n     7\t- `tests/test_release.py`: tests 26–29, and the format-2 updates to earlier tests;\n     8\t- `release_screen_prepare.py` and `release_screen.mjs`;\n     9\t- the run `poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/`: `screen-expected.json`, `screen-results.json`, `old-1-v8.png`;\n    10\t- the result: `RELEASE-PAGE-RESULT.md`;\n    11\t- the mutants: `release_mutants.py`;\n    12\t- the four-store check: `release_check.py`, run `poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23i/`.\n    13\t\n    14\t## Questions\n    15\t\n    16\t1. **Does the code do what revision 7 specifies?** Name each departure with file:line, and whether it is unsafe.\n    17\t2. **Can the shipped page leak anything not in its data, make a request, or show the reader something other than the frozen screen?**\n    18\t   Look at the actual template and script, not only the design.\n    19\t3. **Do the screen check and its negatives judge what they claim?**\n    20\t   - Is the frozen expectation independent of the page under test?\n    21\t   - Does each negative fail for its own reason?\n    22\t   - Is the \"measured\" CDP behaviour recorded faithfully?\n    23\t4. **Do the claims in `RELEASE-PAGE-RESULT.md` follow from the saved results?**\n    24\t5. **Verdict:** slice 2 accepted, or not accepted with each serious finding. Optional tightenings are listed as optional (AGENTS §5;\n    25\t   further checks against hypothetical CSS were judged optional in 76g/76h because the whole template is pinned).\n    26\t\n    27\t**Out of scope:**\n    28\t- the frozen pieces;\n    29\t- the closed v13s line;\n    30\t- slice 1's accepted internals, unless slice 2 breaks them;\n    31\t- the idea path;\n    32\t- the evidence-summary disagreement;\n    33\t- style.\ntotal 136\ndrwx------@ 83 lchingen  staff   2656 Nov 23 12:05 Default\ndrwx------@ 42 lchingen  staff   1344 Nov 23 12:05 .\n-rw-------@  1 lchingen  staff   4014 Nov 23 12:05 Local State\n-rw-r--r--@  1 lchingen  staff     85 Nov 23 12:05 Variations\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
