{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_44","type":"agent_message","text":"**Verdict: slice 2 is not accepted.** The shipped page shows “Forecast unavailable” above the 1,284 evidence entries for `old-1/v8`. I found no path in the pinned page that reads an outside forecast, turns source text into executable markup, or initiates a request. The blockers are in the browser check. It can report success without establishing three conditions revision 7 requires. [Saved screen result:13](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-results.json:13) · [Expanded screenshot](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/old-1-v8.png)\n\n### 1. The shipped page and package\n\nI checked all four saved screen packages against the current renderer. Each page matches its data byte for byte, and the complete template matches the hash pinned in test 29. The script reads the embedded JSON, creates fixed elements, and assigns quotations and source addresses through `textContent`. The data cannot close its script block. The policy admits the pinned script and style and forbids connections. The package checker reads all three files through one folder handle and compares and hashes the same page bytes. [release.py:464](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:464) · [release.py:516](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:516) · [release.py:534](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:534) · [release.py:548](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:548) · [release.py:569](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/src/hivemind/release.py:569) · [test_release.py:832](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/tests/test_release.py:832)\n\nOne harmless pre-release departure is worth recording. Both versions of the page use format 2, although revision 7 says a changed template gets a new format. The comma correction changed the page hash while the data hash stayed identical. I confirmed that the current checker refuses the earlier page and accepts the final one. The browser profile also lives in the run folder instead of the specified scratchpad, outside the release package. [Design:144](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:144) · [Earlier manifest:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23/old-1/manifest.json:1) · [Final manifest:1](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/old-1/manifest.json:1) · [Browser setup:40](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:40)\n\n### 2. Three acceptance blockers\n\n| Finding | What the check can miss |\n|---|---|\n| **Requests and errors are enforced on only one of five normal browser visits.** | Desktop `old-1` checks both. The phone visit discards both. The two dated pages and the escaping fixture save requests but reject only errors. Their saved lists are clean, but an extra request there would still pass. The phone result has no request or error record to inspect. Revision 7 requires both checks on every page through expansion. [Design:204](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:204) · [Desktop:174](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:174) · [Phone:199](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:199) · [Dated pages:205](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:205) · [Escaping fixture:215](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:215) |\n| **The decisive light-background negative never selects light mode.** | Both marker negatives give the marker identical dark foreground and background colours. Only one selects a scheme, and it selects dark. The other inherits the machine setting. On a dark page, even the previously rejected checker that skips the marker’s own background can flag it. The saved count of 19 therefore does not establish the required result *inside a light card*. The shipped contrast calculation itself correctly starts at the text element. [Design:274](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE.md:274) · [Contrast calculation:87](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:87) · [Negative setup:269](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:269) · [Saved counts:145](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-results.json:145) |\n| **Several checks give credit without establishing the stated reason.** | The escaping fixture calls a quote “visible” when a matching text node exists, even if hidden. The transparent-page negative earns credit for any timeout, including a script failure before a single card exists. The inside-card negative earns credit for any collapsed-page mismatch. Its saved card *does* contain the intended extra forecast line. The transparent result retains only `seconds: null`. Also, the first “collapsed” reading forcibly closes the target, so it cannot certify how the card initially opened for the reader. [Initial reading:143](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:143) · [Quote check:212](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:212) · [Negative verdicts:244](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:244) · [Saved observations:117](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-results.json:117) |\n\n### 3. What the saved evidence supports\n\n- **The frozen expectation is independent.** I re-derived all three expected pages from the accepted format-1 packages. They matched the saved expectation, including each dated question’s own evidence. Its full hash matches the browser result. The two dated cards each showed “Answer: Yes” and one evidence group. [Expectation builder:86](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen_prepare.py:86) · [Saved hash:2](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-results.json:2) · [Rubin card:64](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-results.json:64) · [Firmus card:87](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-results.json:87)\n- **The other negatives have evidence for their intended effects.** The sibling forecast landed outside the card. The clipped-quote and clipping-wrapper copies flagged 1,220 and 1,284 texts respectively. The dark marker check found the marker unreadable. The fetch copy rendered and produced a security error naming port 59999 and `connect-src`. [Negative checks:239](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/release_screen.mjs:239) · [Saved negatives:112](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-results.json:112)\n- **The two-error Chrome observation is faithful to the separate port-8788 probe.** Its output records the document request, a security error naming `default-src`, a JavaScript refusal, and a rendered page. It records no request for the fetch. The final port-59999 run retains only `caught`, `rendered`, and `named`, so the exact event count belongs to the earlier probe. [Probe policy:1](/private/tmp/claude-501/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109/scratchpad/cdp/t.html:1) · [Recorded probe output:119530](/Users/lchingen/.claude/projects/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109.jsonl:119530) · [Final fetch result:112](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-results.json:112)\n- **Two result claims need correction.** The final page is **5,794,595 bytes**. The report quotes the earlier page’s 5,794,575. Both meet budget. The four-store run also gives two distinct refusal reasons. The forged evidence summary failed comparison with the store. The forged manifest failed because `note` is outside its allowed fields. [Report:30](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE-RESULT.md:30) · [Reported size:44](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/RELEASE-PAGE-RESULT.md:44) · [Final size:29](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-results.json:29) · [Both refusals:44598](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-check-2026-11-23i/results.json:44598)\n- **The remaining headline measurements hold.** The desktop list rendered in 0.046 seconds. On the 390-pixel phone screen, the Morningstar quote occupied five lines between pixels 36 and 374. The final test output records 429 passing tests, 40 passing release tests, 37 of 38 code mutants caught, and a passing four-store check. [Desktop timing:5](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-results.json:5) · [Phone measurements:48](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/poc/data/release-screen-2026-11-23b/screen-results.json:48) · [Final test output:120140](/Users/lchingen/.claude/projects/-Users-lchingen-hivemind/f1ea972d-85a1-4f27-8010-cf0b60054109.jsonl:120140)\n\n**Recommendation:** correct the browser check and run it once against the same pinned page and frozen expectation. The decisive light-mode test should record a light card around the unreadable dark marker. All normal visits should retain their requests and errors, and each negative should retain the observation that earned it credit. Further hypothetical CSS checks remain optional under 76h. This review was read-only. [Council 76h:6](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-22-number-answers/codex-r76h.md:6)"}}
